# The core's domains, as gosh carries it (REQ21/SHAPE-1): read by the lint over the program as it is
# built (.build/core: the core with the seam's patches, gosh's parts beside it), by the rule a domain
# alone (RULES="a domain"; tools/proofs.sh). The cipher (seam 12), the transport (14), state sync (15) and the terminal (16) are laid out; the rest is
# named, each directory a domain whose ABI is every header (`| *`), until each is laid out in turn.
# gosh's own parts are one domain here: each is held to its own domains by src/DOMAINS, every run.
Crypto        src/crypto
core-include  src/include | *
core-protobufs src/protobufs | *
core-util     src/util | *
Terminal      src/terminal
Network       src/network
StateSync     src/statesync
core-frontend src/frontend | *
core-examples src/examples | *
core-tests    src/tests | *
core-fuzz     src/fuzz | *
gosh          src/command src/copy src/forwarding src/meetup src/pathfinding src/relay src/seam src/ssh src/strong src/stun | *
vendor        vendor | *
allow src/meetup/ticket.h  Crypto  # gosh's raw_key: base64 of 16 bytes, until the cipher's ABI makes a key of them
allow src/crypto/imp/ae.h  Crypto  # OCB's interface (Krovetz's), in C: its struct is declared as C declares it, in no namespace
